+#+TITLE: Patch workflow
+
+How to run the lab-devel patch workflow with the tooling that exists
+today.  zib/patch-review-workflow.org gives the reasoning behind it.
+
+* Model
+- The list is a maildir, =maildir/=, on the =mail= bookmark.  To send
+  a message, deliver it into the maildir, commit it, and push.  There
+  is no SMTP.
+- =trunk= and =mail= share no history.  Each has its own jj workspace
+  in one repo.
+- =upstream= (=/data/lab.git= in a jail) holds the canonical =trunk=
+  and =mail=.  Only the maintainer moves them.
+- =submissions= (=/data/lab-submissions.git=) is the contributor's
+  outbox.  A contributor pushes one bookmark there, named for their
+  login, which holds message commits on top of =mail=.
+
+| Path               | Workspace | Based on |
+|--------------------+-----------+----------|
+| =~/lab/default.jj= | default   | =trunk=  |
+| =~/lab/mail.jj=    | mail      | =mail=   |
+
+* Setup
+** notmuch
+#+BEGIN_SRC sh
+cd ~/lab/default.jj/dotfiles/notmuch
+just install
+#+END_SRC
+
+This installs the hooks into =~/.config/notmuch/default/hooks= and
+copies =notmuch-config.sample= to =~/.notmuch-config= if that file
+does not exist.  Set your identity, then index:
+
+#+BEGIN_SRC sh
+notmuch config set user.name "Your Name"
+notmuch config set user.primary_email you@example.com
+notmuch new
+#+END_SRC
+
+The sample config sets these, and the workflow depends on them:
+- =database.mail_root= is =lab/mail.jj/maildir=.
+- =maildir.synchronize_flags= is false, so notmuch never renames
+  files on the list.
+- =new.tags= is empty, so the hook sets every tag.
+- =index.header.changeid= is =Change-Id=, which makes =changeid:= a
+  search term.
+
+** Contributor jail
+=~claude/bootstrap.sh= (from jails/instances/lab-claude/dist) sets up
+everything above.  It clones =upstream= into =~/lab/default.jj=, adds
+=submissions= as a remote and as the default push remote, tracks
+=trunk@upstream= and =mail@upstream=, adds the mail workspace at
+=~/lab/mail.jj=, installs the notmuch package, and takes the identity
+from =.gitconfig=.  Running it again is safe.
+
+** Emacs
+dotfiles/emacs sets =sendmail-program= to =maildir-deliver.sh=.  A
+message sent from notmuch-emacs therefore lands in the list maildir.
+
+* Tags
+=notmuch new= runs the =post-new= hook, =mail-tag.sh=, which works out
+every tag from the list itself.  The database holds no state of its
+own.  If you rebuild it, the same tags come back.
+
+| Tag       | Meaning                                                  |
+|-----------+----------------------------------------------------------|
+| =sent=    | from =user.primary_email= or =user.other_email=          |
+| =inbox=   | from someone else, and none of your mail replies to it   |
+| =replied= | from someone else, and your mail names it in In-Reply-To |
+
+Messages under =drafts/= get none of these tags.  The =pre-new= hook
+deletes drafts tagged =deleted= and nothing else.  To clear a message
+from your inbox, reply to it.  Tagging it by hand does not last.
+
+Useful searches:
+
+#+BEGIN_SRC sh
+notmuch search --sort=oldest-first tag:inbox
+notmuch search changeid:<jj change id>   # every version of a patch
+notmuch show --entire-thread=true id:<message-id>
+#+END_SRC
+
+* Sending mail
+=libexec/mail/maildir-deliver.sh= reads one message on stdin and files
+it into =$MAILDIR=, or else into notmuch's =mail_root=.  It keeps the
+From header, adds a Date if there is none, and drops a leading mbox
+=From= line.  It does not commit anything.
+
+After delivering, commit in =~/lab/mail.jj=:
+
+#+BEGIN_SRC sh
+jj diff --summary     # only "A maildir/..." lines
+just commit-mail
+#+END_SRC
+
+=just commit-mail= is in the Justfile on =mail=.  It commits each new
+file under =maildir/= on its own, as =msg: <Subject>=.  That lets the
+moderator take or leave each message separately.
+
+** Reply
+In notmuch-emacs, reply and send as usual.  Without Emacs:
+
+#+BEGIN_SRC sh
+notmuch reply --reply-to=all id:<message-id> >/tmp/reply.eml
+# Edit the file and add a Message-ID header.
+libexec/mail/maildir-deliver.sh </tmp/reply.eml
+#+END_SRC
+
+** Patch series
+Post the series as a new thread, not as a reply.  Run
+=libexec/mail/format-patch.sh= with the arguments you would give =git
+format-patch=.  It must write files, not use =--stdout=.  It adds each
+commit's jj change id to every patch, once as a =Change-Id= header and
+once as a =change-id:= line under the =---=.  =git am= drops both.
+
+#+BEGIN_SRC sh
+cd ~/lab/default.jj
+base="$(jj log -r trunk@upstream --no-graph -T commit_id)"
+head="$(jj log -r @- --no-graph -T commit_id)"
+rm -rf /tmp/series
+libexec/mail/format-patch.sh -o /tmp/series --thread=shallow \
+    --base="${base}" --to=<recipient> [--cover-letter] [-v N] \
+    "${base}..${head}"
+for p in /tmp/series/*.patch; do
+	libexec/mail/maildir-deliver.sh <"${p}"
+done
+#+END_SRC
+
+- Always pass =--base=.  It adds a =base-commit:= line.
+- If the series builds on another unmerged series, start the range at
+  that series' head.  git then adds =prerequisite-patch-id:= lines.
+- Post a revision as =-v N= in a new thread.  The change ids stay the
+  same across versions.  In the cover letter, say what changed and
+  link to v(N-1) by Message-ID.
+
+=libexec/mail/mail-send.sh= is an alternative.  It wraps =git
+send-email= with =maildir-deliver.sh= as the sendmail command, but it
+does not add change ids.
+
+* Contributor
+Claude does each pass with the =/process-email= skill in
+.claude/skills/process-email.  The skill is the full procedure.  In
+short, a pass does this:
+
+1. Fetch with =jj git fetch --all-remotes=.
+2. Rebase trunk work.  The commits to move are
+   =mine() ~ ::trunk@upstream ~ (::mail@upstream ~ root())::=.  Rebase
+   them onto =trunk@upstream= with =--skip-emptied=, then abandon any
+   patches the maintainer applied with edits.
+3. In =~/lab/mail.jj=, rebase your bookmark onto =mail@upstream= with
+   =--skip-emptied=.  If no pending mail remains, set the bookmark to
+   =mail@upstream= first.  Then run =notmuch new=.
+4. Answer the oldest =tag:inbox= message.  Post any series first, then
+   reply, citing the series.
+5. Push:
+   #+BEGIN_SRC sh
+   jj bookmark set "$(whoami)" -r @-
+   jj git push --remote submissions --bookmark "$(whoami)"
+   #+END_SRC
+
+* Moderator
+The Justfile on =mail= has the moderation recipes.  Run them in
+=~/lab/mail.jj=:
+
+| Recipe         | Does                                                       |
+|----------------+------------------------------------------------------------|
+| =just fetch=   | fetch =submissions=, copy new =claude@submissions= commits in below =@=, abandon any left empty |
+| =just summary= | show the commits in =::@ ~ ::mail=, with their files       |
+| =just advance= | move =mail= to the last described commit in =::@=          |
+| =just push=    | push =mail= to tngl, jails and github, then =jj git export= |
+
+A moderation pass:
+
+#+BEGIN_SRC sh
+just fetch
+just summary            # each commit must only add maildir/ files
+jj abandon <commit>     # reject a message
+just advance
+just push
+#+END_SRC
+
+=fetch= copies commits with =jj duplicate= rather than rebasing them.
+A message stays off the list until you advance over it.  The
+contributor's next rebase drops whatever =mail= took.
+
+The maintainer posts straight to the list.  Send from notmuch-emacs,
+then run =just commit-mail=, =just advance= and =just push=.
+
+* Maintainer
+=just am [workspace]= applies patches piped in on stdin to a jj
+workspace.  The default workspace is the current directory.  Run it
+from notmuch with =|= on a message or a thread:
+
+#+BEGIN_SRC sh
+cd ~/lab/default.jj && jj new trunk
+notmuch show --format=mbox --entire-thread=true id:<cover-id> | just am
+#+END_SRC
+
+- =@= must be empty and have one parent.  The patches go on top of
+  =@-=, and =@= then moves to a new empty change on top of them.
+- Messages with no diff are skipped, such as cover letters and
+  replies.  That lets you pipe in a whole thread at once.
+- If any patch fails, nothing is applied.
+- It works in =~/lab/mail.jj= too, which has no =.git=.
+
+Review and test, and revise the patches if needed.  To accept, move
+=trunk= to the result and run =just push=, which pushes the tracked
+bookmarks to tngl, jails and github.  To reject, abandon the commits.
+Either way, post the outcome to the thread.
+
+* Reference
+| Path                                   | Role                                 |
+|----------------------------------------+--------------------------------------|
+| libexec/mail/maildir-deliver.sh        | deliver one message into the maildir |
+| libexec/mail/format-patch.sh           | git format-patch plus change ids     |
+| libexec/mail/mail-send.sh              | git send-email into the maildir      |
+| libexec/mail/am.sh (=just am=)         | git am into a jj workspace           |
+| dotfiles/notmuch/hooks/mail-tag.sh     | derive sent, inbox, replied          |
+| dotfiles/notmuch/hooks/pre-new         | purge deleted drafts                 |
+| dotfiles/notmuch/notmuch-config.sample | required notmuch settings            |
+| .claude/skills/process-email           | contributor pass                     |
+| Justfile on =mail=                     | =commit-mail= and moderation         |

